+# ADR-0015 — Shared multi-terminal workspace and Git status context
+
+## Status
+
+Accepted for v1.2.19.
+
+## Decision
+
+Wharness exposes one per-Harness-session interactive terminal workspace through both Editor and Agent. The frontend may render that workspace in different surfaces, but terminal state is shared by session and supports multiple logical tabs. Each logical terminal owns cwd, history, output, target selection and input state. Sandbox terminals intentionally target the same backend development sandbox for that session; Host remains a separately confirmed direct target.
+
+Context construction also records a bounded Git working-tree status. Only paths allowed by context path rules are retained, and the Git-status value contributes to the context fingerprint so planner reuse observes staging/index changes.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Switching Editor/Agent does not destroy interactive terminal history or drafts.
+- Multiple terminal tabs do not create multiple Docker/local sandboxes; they multiplex the existing per-session devspace.
+- Resetting the Sandbox is a session-wide operation and frontend cwd state is reset consistently.
+- Git metadata cannot be used to bypass context exclusions, and failure to obtain status is non-fatal.
